EXTENSION "ArM5_The_Cradle_and_The_Crescent_OrderOfSuleiman_VirtuesFlaws" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Cradle & The Crescent - Chapter Three: Order of Suleiman virtues flaws"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-07"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_The_Cradle_and_The_Crescent_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's virtues flaws, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #t0104b0d146986d5dbe0108 ^"Invocation of Names of Power" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tdtcsFn2Qhvmm6rPadswict8 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Major, Supernatural"
            ^"Size" STRING "Major"
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Cradle & The Crescent"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 30
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The sahir is capable of casting a unique type of spell called a Name of Power, which is invented like a summoning spell (see Seasonal Summoning, later in this chapter) but grants a bonus to a subsequently cast spell, similar in scope to those found on the Shape and Material Bonus table. The spell level is equal to five times the bonus; some example Names of Power are given in the nearby insert. If the sahir knows a Name of Power that governs the area of another spell he wishes to cast, he may “utter” (cast) the Name of Power first, and the subsequent spell’s Casting Total receives a bonus equal to that of the Name of Power. Thus, a Name of Power: Shamash can give a bonus to any formula involving light or justice. A sahir may utter any number of applicable Names of Power before casting a spell, but the total bonus cannot exceed his Finesse score. Names of Power can also be used in conjunction with summoning; the Names invoked must match the type of spirit being summoned. Some examples are:\n\nName Type Adad storms, divination Dumuzi livestock, crops Ishtar healing, love Nergal destruction, disease Ninhursag earth Shamash light, justice\n\n*For example, Jasmin knows the Name of Power: Ishtar at Level 20, granting her +4 to healing effects. She utters this formula in the round before a Solomonic Physic formula designed to speed recovery, and receives a +4 bonus to her Casting Total. Jasmin also knows a Level 15 Name of Power: Ninhursag that gives +3 to earth-related effects, and a Level 15 Name of Power: Nergal that gives +3 to destruction-related effects. She wants to summon an earthquake spirit, so takes two rounds to utter both; however, since her Finesse is 5, she receives only +5 to her roll to summon the spirit, rather than +6.*\n\nBotching a Name of Power roll, or a spell affected by a Name of Power, usually attracts the negative attention of the Named being. This Virtue is similar to (and possibly the ancestor of) the Invocation Magic Virtue (*The Mysteries Revised Edition*, page 78).\n\nThe yatus (see Persia, Chapter 8) introduced this Virtue into the Suhhar Sulayman, and they usually call upon the names of the ancient Mesopotamian gods (see Mythic Mesopotamia, Chapter 7)."
    }

    #t8cb058f0812339fa770e9e ^"Sahir" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tdtcsFn2Qhvmm6rPadswict8 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Free, Social Status"
            ^"Size" STRING "Free"
            ^"Category" STRING "Social Status"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Cradle & The Crescent"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 30
        }
        DESCRIPTION "By demonstrating to the Majlis that he can summon a spirit, the character has been accepted into the Suhhar and is affiliated with a magical academy known as a bayt al-hikma, or “house of wisdom.” He is obliged to further the Suhhar’s causes for one season every year, but is supported by them and benefits from increased access to its teachers, books, and vis sources. During character creation, the character may take appropriate Academic or Arcane Abilities.\n\nIf the character does not actually possess the power to summon a spirit, he should take the Dark Secret Story Flaw, as he will be immediately expelled from the Suhhar when this fact is discovered.\n\nThis Virtue should be taken along with another Social Status Virtue or Flaw, to describe the character’s status among non-sahirs."
    }

    #tf6e0978d136b31d5cf5f1c ^"Sihr" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tdtcsFn2Qhvmm6rPadswict8 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Major, Supernatural"
            ^"Size" STRING "Major"
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Cradle & The Crescent"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 30
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This Virtue gives the character an initial score of 0 in the Accelerated Supernatural Ability of (Solomonic) Sihr."
    }

    #t441d50637c8581cf1987ff ^"Solomonic Alchemy" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tdtcsFn2Qhvmm6rPadswict8 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Major, Supernatural"
            ^"Size" STRING "Major"
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Cradle & The Crescent"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 30
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The character gains an Accelerated Supernatural Ability, Solomonic Alchemy, with an initial score of 0."
    }

